  "text_input": "Patient presented with right lower limb swelling and redness for 3 days, associated with high-grade fever and chills. Known case of Chronic Kidney Disease (CKD) Stage V on medical management, Type 2 Diabetes Mellitus (T2DM) for 14 years on insulin, and Systemic Hypertension for 2 years. History of pulmonary tuberculosis 10 years ago. Examination revealed pallor and deranged renal function (Creatinine 9.4, Urea 204). Diagnosed with sepsis secondary to bilateral pyelonephritis, CKD Stage V, and cellulitis of the right lower limb. Managed with IV antibiotics (Meropenem, Vancomycin, Tigecycline), hemodialysis, and insulin.",
